        <section id="faq" class="py-20">
            <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
                <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-center mb-12 text-dark">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
                    <div class="mb-6">
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2 text-primary">What devices are compatible with WriCo?</h3>
                        <p class="text-dark">WriCo is designed for Apple devices and is compatible with iPhone, iPad,
                            and Mac, ensuring you can write wherever inspiration strikes.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="mb-6">
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2 text-primary">Is there a free version of WriCo?</h3>
                        <p class="text-dark">Yes! The core app is free to use, allowing you to organize notes, plots,
                            characters, and more. However, advanced text AI features are available through a
                            subscription, and image generation operates on a credit system.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="mb-6">
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2 text-primary">How does WriCo sync my work across my
                            devices?</h3>
                        <p class="text-dark">WriCo uses iCloud to seamlessly and securely sync your projects across your
                            Apple devices when connected to the internet. Your work is always backed up and accessible.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2 text-primary">What support options are available?</h3>
                        <p class="text-dark">We're here to help! You can reach us at info@writercopilot.app for any
                            questions or support needs.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

